RULING: MIRROR THE HYDRATING ADAPTER, MINIMALLY (option A, with Codex's corrections). Both hiccup BODY walkers convert each element's attribute map the way the Reagent-tier client adapter does, before the shared serialiser runs:
- names on ordinary (non-hyphenated) elements: a keyword or symbol key goes through Reagent's kebab-to-camel rule and then react-dom's prop-to-attribute alias table; a string key goes through the alias table only;
- a hyphenated (custom-element) tag keeps its author names verbatim;
- a keyword or symbol scalar value is written with `name`;
- a class value is joined the Reagent way.
Stripping, the boolean class and the attribute-name grammar then judge the CONVERTED name. The head emitter and the Ring host shell attribute bags are unchanged. No hot-zone file, no new API, no new error id.

