(d) CACHE. The dossier wanted a per-render cache; Codex called it unnecessary. RULED: no cache is required. The dossier's uncached cold cost (370.6 ms per 100k names, about 3.7 µs per name) is not a page-level finding. If a worker measures a real need, the only permitted shape is a per-render cache in the `*tag-name-cache*` style (rf2-ezdwh), NEVER a process-global cache keyed on names, which splatted attacker-controlled keys would grow without bound.

